# Notepad / VS Code "save as" can append .txt — refuse those too.
.env.local.txt
.env.*.txt
# 🔴 And a SUFFIX after `.local` escapes the `.env.*.local` glob entirely — measured
# 2026-08-14: re-minting the QA passwords wrote a `.env.qa.local.bak` holding the OLD
# secrets, and it showed up as a plain untracked file that any `git add -A` would have
# committed. The glob above requires the name to END in `.local`; a backup does not.
.env*.bak
.env*.old
.env*.orig
.env*~
