selcom-capture-*.txt
selcom-email-*.md

# Database backups (npm run db:backup). NEVER committed: even sealed, these are a
# complete copy of every player balance, phone number, NIDA and KYC record on the
# platform. They belong in the encrypted CI artifact / R2 bucket, not in git.
backups/

# The disposable Postgres cluster npm run db:scratch boots for db:verify-backup.
# During a verification run it holds a FULLY RESTORED copy of the money database —
# every balance, phone number, NIDA and KYC record — in plaintext on disk.
.pgscratch/

# QA screenshot output (regenerated by qa:cert-c1 / qa:cert-c3)
.qa-shots/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Live-QA run artifacts — screenshots, shadow samples, build logs. Evidence, not source.
.qa-artifacts/

# ⭐ REGENERABLE SCREENSHOTS. A driver writes these on every run, so committing them grows the
# repo without adding a fact — `shots/` reached 32 MB of which 8 MB was the same few pages shot
# over and over. Anything a script can recreate on demand is ignored here; a screenshot that is
# EVIDENCE for a finding is committed under its own `shots/<FINDING>/` directory and is cited by
# `docs/`, which `npm run test:docs` now checks actually exists.
shots/chrome/
shots/emails/
shots/*.png

# Live-QA session scratch — probe logs, ad-hoc shots, RED/GREEN transcripts. The EVIDENCE
# lives in docs/LIVE-QA-CAMPAIGN.md; these are the raw files it was read from and they are
# regenerated by the scripts in scripts/, so committing them only grows the repo.
.qa-s2*/
.qa-s2*.txt
.qa-s2*.log
/s2?-*.png
# ⚠️ `.qa-s2*` does NOT cover session 30. The pattern was written when the session number
# happened to start with a 2, and the next session's scratch would have been committed
# silently. Widened rather than renamed, so session 29's paths in the campaign doc still hold.
.qa-s3*/
.qa-s3*.txt
.qa-s3*.log
/s3?-*.png
# Jay unit J's drive (`qa:bonus-j`) writes its shots to the repo ROOT, because that is what
# every live drive does — `harness.mjs` defaults SHOT_DIR to "." and no npm script overrides
# it. ⚠️ ROOT-ANCHORED, for the reason the paragraph below spells out: unanchored, `j-*.png`
# would match at any depth and could claim committed evidence under `shots/<FINDING>/`.
/j-*.png
# 🔴 THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING (2026-08-08, session 37). Unanchored, `s2?-*.png`
# matches at ANY depth — so it silently claimed `shots/S27/s27-add-chain.png`, which is
# COMMITTED EVIDENCE cited by LIVE-QA-CAMPAIGN §E-89 and checked by `npm run test:docs`.
# A cleanup that trusted `git ls-files -i` would have deleted a finding's only proof.
# These patterns mean "session scratch dropped in the repo ROOT", so they say so.

# OUTBOUND DESIGN COMMISSIONS — the package we send a designer, and nothing else.
# ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-11: this said "regenerate with `node scripts/build-design-brief.mjs`".
# That script has never existed in the repo (`find . -name 'build-design-brief*'` → nothing), so
# the package was hand-maintained and unregenerable — which is how its README came to tell an
# outside designer that a celebration amount is set in Sora, the row DESIGN_AUTHORITY §M4
# overturned. Assemble a commission from LIVE files at send time; never from a kept snapshot.
# The AUTHORED receiving playbook is versioned at docs/design-brief/INTAKE.md.
# ⛔ A commission NEVER carries a copy of the rulebook, the tokens, or component source — it
#    links to them. See docs/design-system/README.md §0b and `npm run test:design-one-door`.
# ⚠️ `/design-brief/*` not `/design-brief/` — git cannot re-include anything inside an EXCLUDED
# DIRECTORY, so the trailing-slash form makes every `!` rule below silently dead.
/design-brief/*
/design-brief.zip

# EXCEPTION, 2026-08-12: the round-2 review window above is CLOSED — the kit came back, was
# accepted, and is filed at docs/design-system/v3-2026-08-11-landing-discovery/ (tracked
# normally; not under this exclusion). The ONLY tracked files in /design-brief/ are the living
# plan documents below — everything else that lands here (kit zips, extracted deliveries,
# scratch) stays out of git and gets filed to its §0b home or archived to
# F:\50pick-design-archive\.
!/design-brief/PLAN-OF-RECORD.md
!/design-brief/CLEANUP-MANIFEST.md
!/design-brief/00-NEXT-SESSION-PROMPT.md
/design-brief/**/*.zip

# Local playbook + session tooling dropped at the repo root (not build output, not evidence).
# Untracked AND unignored is the dangerous combination — that is how 2.37 MB of screenshots
# nearly went in on a `git add -A`. Ignored so they cannot be swept in by accident.
/*.bundle
/playbook-enable.sql
/run-playbook.cmd
/verify-playbook.cmd

# Anything unzipped at the repo root. A design handover arrived as "New Landing Design/" on
# 2026-08-11: untracked, NOT ignored, 50 files / 2.87 MB, of which 2.37 MB were regenerable
# screenshots that §0b bans from git. It belongs in /design-brief/. These patterns stop the
# next unzip from becoming a commit; they do not excuse leaving it there.
/New Landing Design/
/*-design-handover*/
/*design-handover*.zip

# The identity pack is zipped for handoff; the folder beside it is the source.
docs/design-brief/*.zip
design-brief-ALL.txt
design-brief-lite/

# Live config snapshots taken either side of a deliberate operator change (ops drill).
scripts/live/ops/.cfg-snapshots/
# KYC identity-document evidence shots (qa:kyc-id-seal / qa:kyc-id-review /
# qa:kyc-id-looked-at, SHOT_DIR=.qa-kyc-id). Same rule as .qa-design/ and .qa-board/:
# the DRIVER is committed so the seal can be re-shot against production for any of the
# four documents, at any width and locale; the PNGs are not, because a checked-in
# screenshot is a claim nobody can re-derive.
.qa-kyc-id/
